1
00:00:01,929 --> 00:00:07,247
[海洋可再生能源概述] Producing enough energy to meet our needs has become a serious problem.

2
00:00:07,247 --> 00:00:15,315
Demand is rising rapidly, because of the world's increasing population and expanding industry.

3
00:00:15,315 --> 00:00:24,597
Burning fossil fuels, like gas, coal and oil, seriously damages the environment and they'll eventually run out.

4
00:00:24,597 --> 00:00:36,854
For a number of years now, scientists have been working out how we can derive energy from renewable sources, such as the sun and wind, without causing pollution.

5
00:00:36,854 --> 00:00:47,951
Today I'll outline marine renewable energy - also called ocean energy - which harnesses the movement of the oceans.

6
00:00:47,951 --> 00:01:04,593
Marine renewable energy can be divided into three main categories: wave energy, tidal energy and ocean thermal energy conversion, and I'll say a few words about each one.

7
00:01:04,593 --> 00:01:07,688
[波浪能的潜力与局限] First, wave energy.

8
00:01:07,688 --> 00:01:23,693
Numerous devices have been invented to harvest wave energy, with names such as Wave Dragon, the Penguin and Mighty Whale, and research is going on to try and come up with a really efficient method.

9
00:01:23,693 --> 00:01:33,774
This form of energy has plenty of potential, as the source is constant, and there's no danger of waves coming to a standstill.

10
00:01:33,774 --> 00:01:43,025
Electricity can be generated using onshore systems, using a reservoir, or offshore systems.

11
00:01:43,025 --> 00:01:52,481
But the problem with ocean waves is that they're erratic, with the wind making them travel in every direction.

12
00:01:52,481 --> 00:02:05,046
This adds to the difficulty of creating efficient technology: ideally all the waves would travel smoothly and regularly along the same straight line.

13
00:02:05,046 --> 00:02:17,305
Another drawback is that sand and other sediment on the ocean floor might be stopped from flowing normally, which can lead to environmental problems.

14
00:02:17,305 --> 00:02:24,056
[潮汐能与潟湖条件] The second category of marine energy that I'll mention is tidal energy.

15
00:02:24,056 --> 00:02:39,178
One major advantage of using the tide, rather than waves, as a source of energy is that it's predictable: we know the exact times of high and low tides for years to come.

16
00:02:39,178 --> 00:02:55,292
For tidal energy to be effective, the difference between high and low tides needs to be at least five metres, and this occurs naturally in only about forty places on Earth.

17
00:02:55,292 --> 00:03:06,250
But the right conditions can be created by constructing a tidal lagoon, an area of sea water separated from the sea.

18
00:03:06,250 --> 00:03:12,948
One current plan is to create a tidal lagoon on the coast of Wales.

19
00:03:12,948 --> 00:03:24,321
This will be an area of water within a bay at Swansea, sheltered by a U-shaped breakwater, or dam, built out from the coast.

20
00:03:24,321 --> 00:03:40,874
[潮汐潟湖如何发电] The breakwater will contain sixteen hydro turbines, and as the tide rises, water rushes through the breakwater, activating the turbines, which turn a generator to produce electricity.

21
00:03:40,874 --> 00:03:56,482
Then, for three hours as the tide goes out, the water is held back within the break water, increasing the difference in water level, until it's several metres higher within the lagoon than in the open sea.

22
00:03:56,482 --> 00:04:04,770
Then, in order to release the stored water, gates in the breakwater are opened.

23
00:04:04,770 --> 00:04:17,846
It pours powerfully out of the lagoon, driving the turbines in the breakwater in the opposite direction and again generating thousands of megawatts of electricity.

24
00:04:17,846 --> 00:04:37,970
As there are two high tides a day, this lagoon scheme would generate electricity four times a day, every day, for a total of around 14 hours in every 24 - and enough electricity for over 150,000 homes.

25
00:04:37,970 --> 00:04:55,807
[潮汐能的效益与风险] This system has quite a lot in its favour: unlike solar and wind energy it doesn't depend on the weather; the turbines are operated without the need for fuel, so it doesn't create any greenhouse gas emissions; and very little maintenance is needed.

26
00:04:55,807 --> 00:05:10,761
It's estimated that electricity generated in this way will be relatively cheap, and that manufacturing the components would create more than 2,000 jobs, a big boost to the local economy.

27
00:05:10,761 --> 00:05:26,871
On the other hand, there are fears that lagoons might harm both fish and birds, for example by disturbing migration patterns, and causing a build-up of silt, affecting local ecosystems.

28
00:05:26,871 --> 00:05:37,592
[海洋温差能转换] There are other forms of tidal energy, but I'll go on to the third category of marine energy: ocean thermal energy conversion.

29
00:05:37,592 --> 00:05:52,734
This depends on there being a big difference in temperature between surface water and the water a couple of kilometres below the surface, and this occurs in tropical coastal areas.

30
00:05:52,734 --> 00:06:00,076
The idea is to bring cold water up to the surface using a submerged pipe.

31
00:06:00,076 --> 00:06:02,576
